26:["$","div","3",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"Gloves are not a substitute for hand hygiene, and the same gloves must never move between patients or between a dirty and a clean task on the same patient. Changing gloves after perineal care and before touching a wound — with hand hygiene between — is not excessive caution; it is the difference between care and cross-contamination."]}]
